WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.959 --> 00:00:02.877
[♪ acoustic guitar playing]

2
00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:10.759
[tab clicks]

3
00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:13.763
[♪ "Yahoos and Triangles"
by The Refreshments playing]

4
00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:29.070
♪

5
00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.036
[♪ theme song concludes]

6
00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:38.454
- [Dale slurping]
- Yep.

7
00:00:38.455 --> 00:00:39.705
- [Boomhauer slurping]
- Yep.

8
00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.623
- Yup.
- [phone buzzing]

9
00:00:41.624 --> 00:00:42.708
[phone clicks]

10
00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:44.418
Hello?

11
00:00:44.419 --> 00:00:47.588
Okay. slow down.
It sounds like you're drunk.

12
00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:48.881
Oh. you are drunk.

13
00:00:48.882 --> 00:00:51.759
Do you have a designated driver?

14
00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.053
Oh. you are the designated driver.

15
00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:57.639
Okay. just text me the address
and I'll be right there.

16
00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.308
Who was that? Peggy?

17
00:00:59.309 --> 00:01:00.934
Peggy's in our house.

18
00:01:00.935 --> 00:01:03.729
Why would she call me
to be a designated driver?

19
00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.981
I don't know. she's your wife.

20
00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:08.067
- It was Joe Jack.
- Who?

21
00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:11.236
You remember.
Joe Jack. from Strickland Propane.

22
00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.030
Talkin' 'bout ol' Booda Sack.
and Enrique.

23
00:01:13.031 --> 00:01:15.157
and then you got 'em
dang ol' Joe Jack. man. who...

24
00:01:15.158 --> 00:01:16.408
[impersonating]
"Hey. Honey."

25
00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:18.243
[elongated] Oh!

26
00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.037
Joe Jack.

27
00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:22.998
I haven't seen
or heard from him in years.

28
00:01:22.999 --> 00:01:26.627
- It's weird that he called me.
- Well. it's not weird to me. Hank.

29
00:01:26.628 --> 00:01:29.005
You're the first one
I'd call if I was drunk.

30
00:01:29.964 --> 00:01:31.632
- Hank?
- Yeah?

31
00:01:31.633 --> 00:01:32.800
I'm drunk.

32
00:01:32.801 --> 00:01:35.677
[groans]
I gotta go pick up Joe Jack.

33
00:01:35.678 --> 00:01:38.305
I'll drive ya. Hank!
We need more beer!

34
00:01:38.306 --> 00:01:39.598
[Hank Hill] No. Bill.

35
00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:41.851
[♪ upbeat country music playing]

36
00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:45.854
Joe Jack... fellas...
what's going on?

37
00:01:45.855 --> 00:01:50.109
Sorry I had to bring you here
under false pretenses. Honey.

38
00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:52.486
We're all drunk. Hank!

39
00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:55.197
We're depressed about what's goin' on
at Strickland Propane.

40
00:01:55.198 --> 00:01:58.868
But how can you be depressed
when you work with propane?

41
00:01:59.577 --> 00:02:01.870
Both of ya better sit down. Honey.

42
00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:04.748
You really are plastered. Joe Jack.

43
00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:09.128
Hank. Strickland is fixing to go under.

44
00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:12.464
Got dangit.
How could Buck let this happen?

45
00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:14.216
Well. that's why we called you.

46
00:02:14.217 --> 00:02:17.469
Can you talk to Buck?
You're the only person he'll listen to.

47
00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:19.972
We know this is a big ask.

48
00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:24.184
considerin' how everything
went down when you... you know.

49
00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:25.478
[♪ dramatic guitar strumming]

50
00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:27.479
Fellas. it's okay.

51
00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:30.274
Buck and I have had dealings
since I've been back.

52
00:02:30.275 --> 00:02:33.569
We just have an unspoken agreement
to bury our feelings

53
00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:36.488
and to never mention... that day.

54
00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.073
[♪ mysterious music plays]

55
00:02:38.074 --> 00:02:41.327
Uh. can you excuse me for a second?
I need to use the restroom.

56
00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.787
What did I tell you?

57
00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:47.040
Buy him a drink first.
and <i>then</i> mention that day.

58
00:02:47.041 --> 00:02:48.417
Sorry. Honeys.

59
00:02:48.418 --> 00:02:51.004
- [♪ light country music playing in bar]
- [patrons chattering]

60
00:02:53.673 --> 00:02:56.008
Excuse me. can I borrow a cigarette?

61
00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:58.510
Borrow?
You mean bum?

62
00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.180
No. maybe.
See. I'm not a smoker.

63
00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:03.640
but all of a sudden.
I feel like havin' a cigarette.

64
00:03:03.641 --> 00:03:06.435
Careful.
That's how I got started.

65
00:03:06.436 --> 00:03:09.563
And ten years later.
I have a porn addiction.

66
00:03:09.564 --> 00:03:12.984
I don't think that has anything
to do with-- never mind.

67
00:03:13.735 --> 00:03:14.818
[lighter clicks]

68
00:03:14.819 --> 00:03:16.361
[inhales sharply]

69
00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:17.696
[exhaling loudly]

70
00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:20.158
[♪ gentle guitar music playing]

71
00:03:20.992 --> 00:03:22.326
[grill sizzling]

72
00:03:22.327 --> 00:03:24.870
You taste the meat. but not the heat.

73
00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:26.873
That's the Strickland guarantee.

74
00:03:28.666 --> 00:03:30.375
Hey. everybody!

75
00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:33.128
Hank just sold his 2.000th grill!

76
00:03:33.129 --> 00:03:34.254
- Yeah!
- Woo-hoo.

77
00:03:34.255 --> 00:03:35.547
- Attaboy. Hank.
- Slam dunk!

78
00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:39.593
Thanks. but the Vogner
Char-King Imperial sells itself.

79
00:03:39.594 --> 00:03:41.221
There's no need to make a fuss.

80
00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:44.723
What am I supposed to do with this?!

81
00:03:44.724 --> 00:03:47.851
Yep. four of a kind
beats three of a kind.

82
00:03:47.852 --> 00:03:49.603
Alright. bye.
Sorry!

83
00:03:49.604 --> 00:03:52.606
That was my bastard son. Ray Roy.

84
00:03:52.607 --> 00:03:55.192
He's gettin' ready
for a business meetin'.

85
00:03:55.193 --> 00:03:57.611
Sounds like you gave him
good advice. sir.

86
00:03:57.612 --> 00:03:58.695
You wanted to see me?

87
00:03:58.696 --> 00:04:01.698
Hank. you and I go way back.

88
00:04:01.699 --> 00:04:04.952
Now. I could tell the moment
you measured my inseam

89
00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:07.329
five times at the Jean Barn

90
00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.916
that your attention to detail
made you a perfect fit

91
00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:12.709
for the propane bid-ness.

92
00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:16.129
Can't thank you enough
for givin' me the opportunity. sir.

93
00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.965
It's been a wild ride.

94
00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:19.841
It certainly has. ol' top.

95
00:04:19.842 --> 00:04:23.637
That's why I think it's time
to let someone else

96
00:04:23.638 --> 00:04:26.890
take over the reins
of Strickland Propane.

97
00:04:26.891 --> 00:04:30.686
So. in a couple of days.
I'm gonna make an announcement.

98
00:04:30.687 --> 00:04:34.189
I just wanted you to know first.

99
00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.691
Well. I'm honored. sir.

100
00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:39.194
But I gotta say.
it's not gonna be the same without you.

101
00:04:39.195 --> 00:04:41.947
Save your butt-smoochin'
for the announcement.

102
00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:43.073
Yes. sir.

103
00:04:43.074 --> 00:04:44.283
[softly] And thank you.

104
00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:47.244
You know ol' Buck
will always take care of ya.

105
00:04:47.245 --> 00:04:50.205
- I know. sir.
- [phone ringing]

106
00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:51.832
Hello?

107
00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:56.670
No. Ray Roy. those shapes
on the cards is diamonds!

108
00:04:56.671 --> 00:04:57.797
♪

109
00:04:59.424 --> 00:05:01.049
- [♪ upbeat guitar music plays]
- [Peggy gasps]

110
00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.801
You are going to be a manager?!

111
00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:06.722
That means I will be the first lady
of Strickland Propane.

112
00:05:06.723 --> 00:05:10.309
Well. it's not official yet.
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

113
00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:14.771
Although. I may splurge and buy myself
a new pair of work jeans.

114
00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:17.941
Oh. Hank.
I was so excited by your news.

115
00:05:17.942 --> 00:05:21.236
that I almost forgot to tell you
not to kill Bobby.

116
00:05:21.237 --> 00:05:23.405
- Why would I kill Bobby?
- [Bobby Hill] Hey. Dad.

117
00:05:23.406 --> 00:05:24.990
Can I borrow the truck?

118
00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:28.535
Only if you're driving
directly to the barbershop

119
00:05:28.536 --> 00:05:29.995
to shave your head.

120
00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.580
Mom! Ugh!

121
00:05:31.581 --> 00:05:33.498
You said you'd talk to him first!

122
00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.375
Peggy. you're okay with this?

123
00:05:35.376 --> 00:05:38.962
He is a 16-year-old.
He is expressing himself.

124
00:05:38.963 --> 00:05:43.884
When I was 16. we expressed ourselves
by listening to our parents.

125
00:05:43.885 --> 00:05:47.220
Well. say goodbye to any chance
of getting a summer job.

126
00:05:47.221 --> 00:05:50.807
No one's gonna wanna hire someone
who looks like a pilot light.

127
00:05:50.808 --> 00:05:54.644
You know who has blue hair
and doesn't have a problem making money?

128
00:05:54.645 --> 00:05:57.064
Jungkook from BTS!

129
00:05:57.065 --> 00:06:01.234
If Joan-Cook from PBS jumped off
a bridge. would you follow her?

130
00:06:01.235 --> 00:06:03.195
Mom! Ugh!

131
00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:05.322
That boy will never be right.

132
00:06:05.323 --> 00:06:07.240
[Buck Strickland]
Okay. listen up.

133
00:06:07.241 --> 00:06:10.370
Propane is a young man's game.

134
00:06:11.329 --> 00:06:14.122
And what with this
Me Too movement in California.

135
00:06:14.123 --> 00:06:18.502
I think it's the right time for me
to take a step back.

136
00:06:18.503 --> 00:06:20.754
- [all whispering]
- We know it's Hank.

137
00:06:20.755 --> 00:06:23.048
Ray Roy. get your butt out here.

138
00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:27.135
Ladies and gents. this is your new
Strickland Propane...

139
00:06:27.136 --> 00:06:28.470
- [♪ dramatic music plays]
- ...manager!

140
00:06:28.471 --> 00:06:30.222
[echoing]
Manager! Manager!

141
00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:32.308
- Thank you. Daddy.
- [employees murmuring]

142
00:06:33.476 --> 00:06:37.229
Sir. I thought Ray Roy was running
Strickland North across town.

143
00:06:37.230 --> 00:06:39.147
Well. that went tits up!

144
00:06:39.148 --> 00:06:42.567
But. it's because he didn't have
someone like you. Hank.

145
00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.277
to help him run the joint.

146
00:06:44.278 --> 00:06:46.613
But you said you were
gonna take care of me. sir.

147
00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:49.950
I am.
You gonna be Ray Roy's number two.

148
00:06:49.951 --> 00:06:52.285
See. that's what you do best. Hank.

149
00:06:52.286 --> 00:06:54.413
You're a natural lieutenant.

150
00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:57.374
If you weren't here. hell.
I wouldn't trust Ray Roy

151
00:06:57.375 --> 00:07:00.961
to pour piss out of a boot
if the instructions was on the heel!

152
00:07:00.962 --> 00:07:04.172
But. sir. I've been here 20 years.

153
00:07:04.173 --> 00:07:07.717
I only came in late once.
and that was the day Bobby was born.

154
00:07:07.718 --> 00:07:08.885
Exactly!

155
00:07:08.886 --> 00:07:11.721
You're my ace in the hole. Hank.
my linchpin.

156
00:07:11.722 --> 00:07:15.016
Yeah! And now you're <i>my</i> linchpin.
whatever that means.

157
00:07:15.017 --> 00:07:16.768
With all due respect. sir.

158
00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:20.480
giving the business to him
is like givin' a gun to a monkey.

159
00:07:20.481 --> 00:07:22.357
or-- or worse. a Ray Roy.

160
00:07:22.358 --> 00:07:24.609
Hey. I'm your boss now.

161
00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:27.279
The only thing this "monkey"
will be firing is you.

162
00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.655
if you don't watch your step.

163
00:07:28.656 --> 00:07:30.115
- Huh?
- Mm.

164
00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:33.452
Well. let me save you the trouble there.
because I quit.

165
00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:34.703
- [Donna hollering]
- [Enrique gasping]

166
00:07:34.704 --> 00:07:36.705
No need to be like that. ol' top.

167
00:07:36.706 --> 00:07:40.334
Yeah. just face the facts.
Blood's thicker than propane.

168
00:07:41.085 --> 00:07:42.419
Actually. it's not.

169
00:07:42.420 --> 00:07:44.880
Propane's four-point-two
pounds per gallon.

170
00:07:44.881 --> 00:07:46.089
blood is half that.

171
00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.883
- It is?
- No.

172
00:07:47.884 --> 00:07:50.844
Only a monkey or a Ray Roy
would fall for that.

173
00:07:50.845 --> 00:07:53.388
- [♪ somber guitar music playing]
- [door slamming]

174
00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:55.975
It's the end of an era. Honey.

175
00:07:59.061 --> 00:08:01.396
[♪ gentle guitar music playing]

176
00:08:01.397 --> 00:08:02.689
What's goin' on. Mom?

177
00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.900
Your father has called a family meeting

178
00:08:04.901 --> 00:08:08.445
to announce that he will be running
Strickland Propane as a manager.

179
00:08:08.446 --> 00:08:09.988
You did not hear it from me.

180
00:08:09.989 --> 00:08:13.366
- So remember. Bobby. act surprised.
- [screen door opens and closes]

181
00:08:13.367 --> 00:08:16.953
Peggy. Bobby. I quit Strickland Propane.

182
00:08:16.954 --> 00:08:18.663
[fake enthusiasm]
Dad. that's great!

183
00:08:18.664 --> 00:08:21.416
Manager?
I'm so proud of you!

184
00:08:21.417 --> 00:08:24.419
No. Bobby. he said he quit.

185
00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:26.129
Oh. Sorry. Dad.

186
00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.964
I was focused on my part.

187
00:08:27.965 --> 00:08:30.175
Can you give it to me again.
from the top?

188
00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:32.177
Hank. what happened?

189
00:08:32.178 --> 00:08:34.679
Buck gave my job to Ray Roy.

190
00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:36.598
Ray Roy?!
Didn't you once say

191
00:08:36.599 --> 00:08:39.643
he used propane to fill balloons
at a children's party?

192
00:08:39.644 --> 00:08:40.936
Uh-huh.

193
00:08:40.937 --> 00:08:43.271
But I don't blame Buck.
I blame myself.

194
00:08:43.272 --> 00:08:44.814
I just saw red.

195
00:08:44.815 --> 00:08:47.025
I heard someone say "I quit."

196
00:08:47.026 --> 00:08:49.653
and then I realized
that someone was me.

197
00:08:49.654 --> 00:08:51.446
I guess I was in denial

198
00:08:51.447 --> 00:08:54.074
about how much I really
wanted to be manager.

199
00:08:54.075 --> 00:08:56.493
Well. while you figure out
what is next for Hank Hill.

200
00:08:56.494 --> 00:08:58.662
your son and I will pick up the slack.

201
00:08:58.663 --> 00:09:01.289
Bobby. it's time for you
to be man of the house.

202
00:09:01.290 --> 00:09:03.291
What?
There's no need for that.

203
00:09:03.292 --> 00:09:05.460
I've been outta work
for less than an hour.

204
00:09:05.461 --> 00:09:09.422
Mom. listen to Dad.
I don't want to be a man.

205
00:09:09.423 --> 00:09:12.592
First thing in the morning.
you are going out to find a job.

206
00:09:12.593 --> 00:09:15.220
It is time for you to nut up. Bobby Hill.

207
00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:18.181
No one needs to "nut up."
especially Bobby.

208
00:09:18.182 --> 00:09:22.769
I have 20 years' experience
in propane and propane accessories.

209
00:09:22.770 --> 00:09:24.313
I'll find a job.

210
00:09:25.106 --> 00:09:29.193
Just to clarify.
do I still have to nut up?

211
00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:31.903
[Hank slurping]

212
00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:33.947
Okay. Hank.
you can come work for me

213
00:09:33.948 --> 00:09:36.825
as an assistant exterminator.

214
00:09:36.826 --> 00:09:39.828
But fair warning.
I'm a hard-nosed boss

215
00:09:39.829 --> 00:09:41.955
that doesn't tolerate slackers.

216
00:09:41.956 --> 00:09:45.709
It's 11:00 a.m.. and you're in the alley
drinking beer. Dale.

217
00:09:45.710 --> 00:09:49.963
That's why I desperately need
an assistant. to help me find work.

218
00:09:49.964 --> 00:09:51.923
Thanks. but no thanks.

219
00:09:51.924 --> 00:09:54.050
So. what are you gonna do. Hank?

220
00:09:54.051 --> 00:09:56.761
Well. there's only one
other propane game in town.

221
00:09:56.762 --> 00:10:01.057
and I'm never gonna work for
"the man who shall remain nameless."

222
00:10:01.058 --> 00:10:02.892
- Thatherton!
- [can crunching]

223
00:10:02.893 --> 00:10:05.770
Last time I said his name.
you kicked my butt.

224
00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:08.481
[chuckles]
But apparently. it's a one-way street

225
00:10:08.482 --> 00:10:10.150
when it comes to butt-kickings.

226
00:10:10.151 --> 00:10:13.361
I haven't had to apply
for a job in over 20 years.

227
00:10:13.362 --> 00:10:16.197
What's the best bond of paper
to print a resume on?

228
00:10:16.198 --> 00:10:17.991
Paper. man? [chuckling]
What are you talkin' 'bout?

229
00:10:17.992 --> 00:10:19.326
You gotta get on ol' LinkedIn. man.

230
00:10:19.327 --> 00:10:22.371
Gotta just upload that. um. info. man.
just. and boom.

231
00:10:23.289 --> 00:10:28.293
Boomhauer. you set your minimum salary
at $400.000 a year?

232
00:10:28.294 --> 00:10:30.629
Hey. man. talkin' 'bout
I'm dang ol' worth it. man.

233
00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:31.631
[slurping]

234
00:10:32.173 --> 00:10:35.383
[Peggy Hill] We should mention
you received a "Blue Flame of Valor."

235
00:10:35.384 --> 00:10:38.011
and that you were
"Propane Salesman of the Year"

236
00:10:38.012 --> 00:10:39.554
for three years running.

237
00:10:39.555 --> 00:10:42.057
Peggy. I don't want to come across
as a braggart.

238
00:10:42.058 --> 00:10:44.893
And I wouldn't wanna work
for a company that would hire one.

239
00:10:44.894 --> 00:10:48.855
Oh. Hank. everyone knows
the truest sign of humility is bragging.

240
00:10:48.856 --> 00:10:50.315
And I am the humblest.

241
00:10:50.316 --> 00:10:53.319
Done.
And now... we wait.

242
00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:55.779
[clicking keys]

243
00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.030
Be patient. Hank.

244
00:10:57.031 --> 00:11:00.450
A job does not suddenly
just walk through the door.

245
00:11:00.451 --> 00:11:03.328
Guess who got a job
at Whataburger?

246
00:11:03.329 --> 00:11:05.789
You're lookin' at their new grill cook.

247
00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:07.499
What?
But how could you?

248
00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:10.669
You're-- you're dressed
like a Korean pop dancer.

249
00:11:10.670 --> 00:11:14.506
The manager was also a K-pop fan.
He has pink hair.

250
00:11:14.507 --> 00:11:19.511
We watched a whole BTS concert
on his laptop during my interview.

251
00:11:19.512 --> 00:11:21.971
- Oh. God.
- I start tonight.

252
00:11:21.972 --> 00:11:25.267
Dad. can you give me a lift
to my shift?

253
00:11:25.768 --> 00:11:28.228
[singing]
<i>♪ Workin' nine to five ♪</i>

254
00:11:28.229 --> 00:11:30.563
<i>♪ Easy way to make a livin' ♪</i>

255
00:11:30.564 --> 00:11:33.316
<i>♪ And there's somethin'. somethin' ♪</i>

256
00:11:33.317 --> 00:11:36.319
<i>- ♪ About givin' ♪</i>
- [screen door opens and closes]

257
00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.864
I bet he's fired
before the end of his shift.

258
00:11:39.865 --> 00:11:42.410
[♪ upbeat country music playing]

259
00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.745
Nothing?

260
00:11:45.746 --> 00:11:48.581
I'd even consider a job in...
[shudders]

261
00:11:48.582 --> 00:11:50.583
...alternative energy.

262
00:11:50.584 --> 00:11:52.794
Hank. we should do
a project together

263
00:11:52.795 --> 00:11:55.088
while you wait for a propane offer!

264
00:11:55.089 --> 00:11:57.257
Maybe even start our own business.

265
00:11:57.258 --> 00:11:59.300
A business?
Like what?

266
00:11:59.301 --> 00:12:01.761
I have always pictured us
opening a school

267
00:12:01.762 --> 00:12:03.513
for magical children.

268
00:12:03.514 --> 00:12:05.390
- You mean gifted?
- Nope.

269
00:12:05.391 --> 00:12:09.728
Mom. Dad. I got my first paycheck!

270
00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:11.646
Now. I know you guys
are worried about money.

271
00:12:11.647 --> 00:12:13.982
so I thought I'd help out.

272
00:12:13.983 --> 00:12:16.234
Wait. who said we were
worried about money?

273
00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:18.278
Mr. Souphanousinphone.

274
00:12:18.279 --> 00:12:19.571
And then. he laughed.

275
00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:22.699
Well. he's wrong.
We're not worried about money.

276
00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:25.660
- Yet.
- Dad. no. I insist.

277
00:12:25.661 --> 00:12:28.830
Feel free to use that
to cover the mortgage.

278
00:12:28.831 --> 00:12:32.876
And if there's anything left over.
buy yourselves something nice.

279
00:12:32.877 --> 00:12:34.919
Well. that is very sweet. Bobby.

280
00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:39.048
But this check would not cover
one night in a Super 8 motel.

281
00:12:39.049 --> 00:12:41.593
or-- or even a regular 8 motel.

282
00:12:41.594 --> 00:12:45.054
Yeah. maybe let it grow up some
before you worry about chipping in.

283
00:12:45.055 --> 00:12:49.810
Um. I'm the only one
with a job in this house.

284
00:12:50.394 --> 00:12:52.730
[♪ gentle guitar music playing]

285
00:12:54.023 --> 00:12:55.608
[sighs]

286
00:12:58.694 --> 00:12:59.904
[door bell jingling]

287
00:13:02.490 --> 00:13:05.784
Well. well. well.
look who came crawlin' back

288
00:13:05.785 --> 00:13:07.577
lookin' for a job.

289
00:13:07.578 --> 00:13:09.913
Enough small talk. Thatherton.

290
00:13:09.914 --> 00:13:11.498
Are you offerin' me one or not?

291
00:13:11.499 --> 00:13:14.959
Well. I could always use someone
with your experience here.

292
00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:17.212
But before we shake on it.
you gotta give me

293
00:13:17.213 --> 00:13:20.673
all the dirt on Strickland
and how he runs his business.

294
00:13:20.674 --> 00:13:23.551
Finally. we can take Buck down together.

295
00:13:23.552 --> 00:13:25.804
Sorry. M.F.. I won't do that.

296
00:13:25.805 --> 00:13:29.642
Even after you quit
and he gave your job to his bastard son?

297
00:13:30.726 --> 00:13:33.478
Dammit.
You have morals. Hank.

298
00:13:33.479 --> 00:13:35.647
But I'll hire you anyway.

299
00:13:35.648 --> 00:13:37.774
I could really use another number two.

300
00:13:37.775 --> 00:13:40.401
What do you mean. <i>another</i> number two?

301
00:13:40.402 --> 00:13:43.613
I'm the number one number two.
Remember that!

302
00:13:43.614 --> 00:13:46.533
You'd really be
the number one number two.

303
00:13:46.534 --> 00:13:49.244
I... I got ears!
I heard that!

304
00:13:49.245 --> 00:13:51.955
There can only be one
number one number two.

305
00:13:51.956 --> 00:13:54.750
And that's me!
You're the number two number two!

306
00:13:55.292 --> 00:13:56.543
Hey!

307
00:13:56.544 --> 00:13:58.962
Hanging up the sign is my job!

308
00:13:58.963 --> 00:14:02.048
The number one number two
hangs the signs!

309
00:14:02.049 --> 00:14:04.218
♪

310
00:14:05.427 --> 00:14:10.098
Okay. before we kill the termites.
we need to understand them.

311
00:14:10.099 --> 00:14:13.476
Lesson one.
the termites' reproduction cycle.

312
00:14:13.477 --> 00:14:16.688
After a passionate night
of fertilization--

313
00:14:16.689 --> 00:14:18.481
[sighs] I quit.

314
00:14:18.482 --> 00:14:21.860
Hank. you got a message
on your LinkedIn profile!

315
00:14:21.861 --> 00:14:24.863
You have an interview
for a propane job in Houston.

316
00:14:24.864 --> 00:14:27.782
See. Peggy?
I told you my years of experience

317
00:14:27.783 --> 00:14:29.951
- would speak for itself.
- About that...

318
00:14:29.952 --> 00:14:32.912
Hank. do not get mad.
but I took the liberty

319
00:14:32.913 --> 00:14:36.457
of making some slight
adjustments to your profile.

320
00:14:36.458 --> 00:14:39.752
Conversational French?
Hang gliding?

321
00:14:39.753 --> 00:14:43.381
And you removed "assistant."
Peggy. they'll think I'm a manager.

322
00:14:43.382 --> 00:14:47.302
Hank. I know you are more
than qualified to be a manager.

323
00:14:47.303 --> 00:14:49.012
Now. they know that too.

324
00:14:49.013 --> 00:14:51.974
But the question is. do <i>you</i> know it?

325
00:14:53.142 --> 00:14:55.184
Peggy. I'm off to Houston.

326
00:14:55.185 --> 00:14:56.311
[♪ inspiring music playing]

327
00:14:56.312 --> 00:15:01.691
There goes the best
Dead Bug employee I ever had.

328
00:15:01.692 --> 00:15:03.401
- including myself.
- [termites scurrying]

329
00:15:03.402 --> 00:15:05.237
- [♪ gentle music playing]
- [people chattering]

330
00:15:05.571 --> 00:15:06.654
[door opens]

331
00:15:06.655 --> 00:15:09.115
Mr. Hill. we're ready for you now.

332
00:15:09.116 --> 00:15:11.117
[with awkward accent]
<i>Merci beaucoup.</i>

333
00:15:11.118 --> 00:15:12.327
[office phones ringing]

334
00:15:12.328 --> 00:15:13.662
[Hank sighs deeply]

335
00:15:15.414 --> 00:15:16.581
[Ladybird panting]

336
00:15:16.582 --> 00:15:18.708
- Leftover hot dogs. Ladybird.
- [chomping]

337
00:15:18.709 --> 00:15:22.795
Ladybird and I were so anxious.
we decided to clean out the fridge.

338
00:15:22.796 --> 00:15:25.882
I think I found Bobby's
seventh-grade science project.

339
00:15:25.883 --> 00:15:28.092
Or maybe it was just a bowl of old gravy.

340
00:15:28.093 --> 00:15:29.636
Well. how did it go?

341
00:15:29.637 --> 00:15:34.015
Peggy. Ladybird. they offered me
a long-term job contract.

342
00:15:34.016 --> 00:15:36.434
With bonuses and a retirement plan.

343
00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:38.770
Oh. Hank. that is so great!

344
00:15:38.771 --> 00:15:42.106
And do not worry.
We will adjust to Houston!

345
00:15:42.107 --> 00:15:44.192
There may be some
culture shock at first--

346
00:15:44.193 --> 00:15:46.152
Peggy. the job's not in Houston.

347
00:15:46.153 --> 00:15:48.738
It's in... Saudi Arabia.

348
00:15:48.739 --> 00:15:50.239
[♪ dramatic music playing]

349
00:15:50.240 --> 00:15:53.701
Please tell me that's what
they're calling El Paso now.

350
00:15:53.702 --> 00:15:55.370
[marker squeaking]

351
00:15:55.371 --> 00:15:59.248
Okay. let's review the pros
and the cons of Saud-i Arabia.

352
00:15:59.249 --> 00:16:02.377
First con. it is in Saud-i Arabia.

353
00:16:02.378 --> 00:16:04.587
Yes. but pro. I get to spread

354
00:16:04.588 --> 00:16:07.132
the gospel of propane to the Middle East.

355
00:16:08.050 --> 00:16:12.512
However. it means leaving Texas.
the only home we've ever known.

356
00:16:12.513 --> 00:16:17.308
But pro. I can teach English
and <i>Español</i> to Saud-i Arabians.

357
00:16:17.309 --> 00:16:19.519
But con. women can't drive

358
00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:22.438
outside the Aramco base in Saudi Arabia.

359
00:16:22.439 --> 00:16:24.608
Although. half the traffic.

360
00:16:25.484 --> 00:16:29.278
Pro. ever since I saw
<i>Lawrence of Arabia</i> as a little girl.

361
00:16:29.279 --> 00:16:31.406
I always wanted to ride a camel.

362
00:16:31.407 --> 00:16:35.034
Hank. so far.
the cons do not outweigh the pros.

363
00:16:35.035 --> 00:16:38.329
Con. [sighs] I'd still only be
an assistant manager.

364
00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:42.000
And another con.
we'd be leaving our friends behind.

365
00:16:42.001 --> 00:16:44.877
But pro. one of them is Kahn.

366
00:16:44.878 --> 00:16:48.840
But con-- and this is the biggest con
of them all-- what about Bobby?

367
00:16:48.841 --> 00:16:51.592
- [♪ pensive guitar music plays]
- Oh. yeah. Bobby.

368
00:16:51.593 --> 00:16:55.763
He would be leaving behind Connie.
and Joseph. and all his other friends.

369
00:16:55.764 --> 00:16:58.725
- Bobby has other friends?
- No. he does not.

370
00:16:58.726 --> 00:17:00.268
I was just being generous.

371
00:17:00.269 --> 00:17:03.938
Peggy. I hate to say it.
but we need to have an adult conversation

372
00:17:03.939 --> 00:17:07.358
with a boy who still watches cartoons
about a sponge.

373
00:17:07.359 --> 00:17:09.069
♪

374
00:17:10.946 --> 00:17:14.283
- [♪ energetic music playing]
- [burgers sizzling]

375
00:17:18.537 --> 00:17:19.872
[bottles spurting]

376
00:17:23.083 --> 00:17:27.086
Two doubles and a Junior with no cheese.
up and ready to go.

377
00:17:27.087 --> 00:17:29.839
This must be Jacob's order.
'Sup. Jacob?

378
00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:31.841
- Can I get some--
- [Bobby] Honey mustard?

379
00:17:31.842 --> 00:17:35.011
You got it.
Puttin' two extra in your takeout bag.

380
00:17:35.012 --> 00:17:37.430
because I know you're a big dipper.

381
00:17:37.431 --> 00:17:38.514
Whoa!

382
00:17:38.515 --> 00:17:41.934
I've never seen Bobby
"in the zone" before.

383
00:17:41.935 --> 00:17:43.437
except when he's napping.

384
00:17:44.813 --> 00:17:47.398
Don't worry about the food.
It's on me.

385
00:17:47.399 --> 00:17:49.984
I get a 50% discount.

386
00:17:49.985 --> 00:17:52.195
So. what'd you wanna talk about?

387
00:17:52.196 --> 00:17:56.032
Must be important.
it's the second family meeting in a month.

388
00:17:56.033 --> 00:17:59.285
- Wait! Is Mom pregnant?
- What? No!

389
00:17:59.286 --> 00:18:03.623
I. uh. I got a job offer in Saudi Arabia.

390
00:18:03.624 --> 00:18:07.293
Saudi Arabia?
Where Lawrence is from?

391
00:18:07.294 --> 00:18:10.129
- Uh-huh.
- Well. that's great. Dad.

392
00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:13.883
So... wait. does that mean
you'll be leaving us?

393
00:18:13.884 --> 00:18:15.259
No. Bobby.

394
00:18:15.260 --> 00:18:18.679
We would all have to move
to Saudi Arabia. as a family.

395
00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:21.682
Oh. I don't want to do that.

396
00:18:21.683 --> 00:18:23.351
I understand. son.

397
00:18:23.352 --> 00:18:26.646
I'll call Aramco and tell 'em
I'm not takin' the job.

398
00:18:26.647 --> 00:18:28.106
No. no. no. no. no. no.

399
00:18:28.107 --> 00:18:30.608
You guys should go.
but I can't leave now.

400
00:18:30.609 --> 00:18:34.904
I have just figured out
what I want to do with my life.

401
00:18:34.905 --> 00:18:37.198
I wanna work in the restaurant business!

402
00:18:37.199 --> 00:18:39.951
- [♪ inspiring music playing]
- I love food. I love people.

403
00:18:39.952 --> 00:18:42.453
and I love people eating my food.

404
00:18:42.454 --> 00:18:45.039
I finally found my propane. Dad.

405
00:18:45.040 --> 00:18:47.375
And propane accessories!

406
00:18:47.376 --> 00:18:50.169
Bobby. we cannot let you stay here. alone.

407
00:18:50.170 --> 00:18:51.462
You would die.

408
00:18:51.463 --> 00:18:53.005
Plus. you need to finish high school.

409
00:18:53.006 --> 00:18:57.176
Mom. I promise I'll finish school
and that I won't die.

410
00:18:57.177 --> 00:18:59.971
I can live with Luanne.
Lucky. and Gracie.

411
00:18:59.972 --> 00:19:01.973
You are their favorite babysitter.

412
00:19:01.974 --> 00:19:04.725
And I promise. we'll Skype every day.

413
00:19:04.726 --> 00:19:06.227
I can visit you!

414
00:19:06.228 --> 00:19:08.437
Mom. Dad. I can do this.

415
00:19:08.438 --> 00:19:10.064
[alarm ringing]

416
00:19:10.065 --> 00:19:13.609
I gotta get back to work.
We'll talk about this more at home.

417
00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:15.736
Relax. enjoy your meal.

418
00:19:15.737 --> 00:19:19.074
and I'll go get you
some hot apple pies to go.

419
00:19:19.867 --> 00:19:22.076
Am I feeling... pride?

420
00:19:22.077 --> 00:19:25.204
I guess our boy
has finally nutted up. Hank.

421
00:19:25.205 --> 00:19:26.373
I guess so.

422
00:19:28.041 --> 00:19:30.793
Oh. no.
You know who won't take this well?

423
00:19:30.794 --> 00:19:32.045
[knocking]

424
00:19:33.046 --> 00:19:34.547
Hank. Peggy!

425
00:19:34.548 --> 00:19:36.424
[laughing] Come in.

426
00:19:36.425 --> 00:19:39.136
What an unexpected surprise.

427
00:19:41.346 --> 00:19:43.723
[Bill screaming]
No!

428
00:19:43.724 --> 00:19:45.100
[Bill sobbing]

429
00:19:45.309 --> 00:19:48.312
[♪ gentle guitar music playing]

430
00:19:58.447 --> 00:20:01.365
Okay. fellas. [sighs]
I'll talk to Buck for ya.

431
00:20:01.366 --> 00:20:04.161
Knew we could count on you. Honey.

432
00:20:05.204 --> 00:20:08.247
Have a seat. ol' top.
Can I get you somethin' to drink?

433
00:20:08.248 --> 00:20:10.541
This isn't a social call. sir.

434
00:20:10.542 --> 00:20:13.252
What I have to say
is best said while standing.

435
00:20:13.253 --> 00:20:16.214
I'm here on behalf
of Joe Jack. Booda Sack--

436
00:20:16.215 --> 00:20:18.007
Say no more. let me guess.

437
00:20:18.008 --> 00:20:20.718
They're tellin' you the company
is goin' "bankrupt."

438
00:20:20.719 --> 00:20:24.597
and it's all because
of "my bastard son." Ray Roy.

439
00:20:24.598 --> 00:20:27.892
Well. guess what. Hank?
They're right!

440
00:20:27.893 --> 00:20:31.145
Got dangit. Buck.
How could you let it get this bad?

441
00:20:31.146 --> 00:20:34.523
You can't treat your staff like this.
That's why I quit.

442
00:20:34.524 --> 00:20:37.860
They're the victims here.
not to mention propane.

443
00:20:37.861 --> 00:20:40.905
That gas has been nothing
but good to you. sir.

444
00:20:40.906 --> 00:20:42.406
I know!

445
00:20:42.407 --> 00:20:45.326
But I can't fire him. Hank.
I've tried!

446
00:20:45.327 --> 00:20:49.497
Ray Roy's my kryptonite.
and he's my only family.

447
00:20:49.498 --> 00:20:51.874
Well. that's where you're wrong. Buck.

448
00:20:51.875 --> 00:20:55.878
I worked for Aramco.
the largest oil producer in the world.

449
00:20:55.879 --> 00:20:59.215
But Strickland Propane had something
Aramco didn't have.

450
00:20:59.216 --> 00:21:00.508
family.

451
00:21:00.509 --> 00:21:02.009
Ray Roy isn't your legacy.

452
00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:04.387
the whole Strickland Propane team is.

453
00:21:04.388 --> 00:21:07.974
You've gotta nut up
and fire Ray Roy. Buck.

454
00:21:07.975 --> 00:21:10.393
You're right. ol' top.

455
00:21:10.394 --> 00:21:11.894
Can you do it for me?

456
00:21:11.895 --> 00:21:13.646
I don't work for you now. sir.

457
00:21:13.647 --> 00:21:16.565
- And I never will again.
- Please. Hank. please!

458
00:21:16.566 --> 00:21:19.318
Save our family. huh?
Be the daddy!

459
00:21:19.319 --> 00:21:22.154
I-- I know I did ya wrong. but come back!

460
00:21:22.155 --> 00:21:23.656
You be the daddy!

461
00:21:23.657 --> 00:21:26.242
Please. be the daddy!
[whimpering]

462
00:21:26.243 --> 00:21:30.414
Have some respect.
and stop kissing my shoes.

463
00:21:31.498 --> 00:21:34.292
[Peggy gasps]
You said no? To Buck?

464
00:21:34.293 --> 00:21:36.127
Uh-huh.

465
00:21:36.128 --> 00:21:37.713
Buck Strickland?

466
00:21:39.381 --> 00:21:40.798
Well. good.

467
00:21:40.799 --> 00:21:43.175
I know that that was hard
for you to do. Hank.

468
00:21:43.176 --> 00:21:44.719
seeing how you love propane

469
00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:47.389
- almost as much as you love me.
- Yep.

470
00:21:48.348 --> 00:21:50.224
Well. what the heck did Buck expect?

471
00:21:50.225 --> 00:21:53.227
He should have promoted you
back when he had the chance.

472
00:21:53.228 --> 00:21:55.980
Well. the way I look at it. Peggy.
we never would've gone

473
00:21:55.981 --> 00:21:58.316
to Saudi Arabia
and secured our nest egg.

474
00:21:58.317 --> 00:22:00.443
Bobby wouldn't have found his passion.

475
00:22:00.444 --> 00:22:03.654
and-- and you wouldn't have had
a chance to ride <i>two</i> camels.

476
00:22:03.655 --> 00:22:08.159
And I met a prince.
who I am pretty sure fell in love with me.

477
00:22:08.160 --> 00:22:09.577
Mm-hmm.

478
00:22:09.578 --> 00:22:11.829
[♪ gentle music playing]

479
00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:13.664
We better step on it.

480
00:22:13.665 --> 00:22:17.001
Bobby said he'd only hold
our reservation for 15 minutes.

481
00:22:17.002 --> 00:22:20.713
You'd think he would give us more time.
seeing that I gave birth to him.

482
00:22:20.714 --> 00:22:22.257
[Hank sighs]

483
00:22:23.091 --> 00:22:25.509
Hank. you sure
you wanna turn down here?

484
00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:27.511
We always go the long way. ever since--

485
00:22:27.512 --> 00:22:31.265
It's okay. Peggy.
That chapter's finally closed.

486
00:22:31.266 --> 00:22:33.059
I'm just Hank Hill. citizen.

487
00:22:33.060 --> 00:22:36.021
driving past a local propane business.

488
00:22:36.521 --> 00:22:37.856
[♪ dramatic music playing]

489
00:22:38.357 --> 00:22:39.732
Sickland?!

490
00:22:39.733 --> 00:22:42.943
What twisted bastard
thought that'd be funny?

491
00:22:42.944 --> 00:22:45.112
Well. maybe it's supposed
to be a good thing.

492
00:22:45.113 --> 00:22:47.531
- I hear "sick" means cool.
- [tires screeching]

493
00:22:47.532 --> 00:22:49.867
That storage unit needs to be locked up!

494
00:22:49.868 --> 00:22:52.370
That's a blatant code violation!

495
00:22:52.371 --> 00:22:55.790
It's like a gotdang horror movie.

496
00:22:55.791 --> 00:22:59.293
- You're going inside. aren't you?
- Yeah. [sighs] you're right. Peggy.

497
00:22:59.294 --> 00:23:00.837
[sighs] I should.

498
00:23:01.296 --> 00:23:03.130
- [door creaking]
- [liquid dripping]

499
00:23:03.131 --> 00:23:05.549
Bwah! Is that urine?

500
00:23:05.550 --> 00:23:07.176
In the showroom?

501
00:23:07.177 --> 00:23:10.180
[♪ tense music playing]

502
00:23:11.181 --> 00:23:13.475
[loud snoring]

503
00:23:17.104 --> 00:23:18.105
Is he dead?

504
00:23:19.606 --> 00:23:21.691
I didn't know she was your wife!

505
00:23:21.983 --> 00:23:23.359
[booze bottle sloshing]

506
00:23:23.360 --> 00:23:25.403
- Peggy.
- I understand.

507
00:23:25.404 --> 00:23:26.862
- [birds squawking]
- [camera clicking]

508
00:23:26.863 --> 00:23:29.866
[♪ "Mainstreet" by Bob Seger playing]

509
00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:35.204
Shouldn't it say "owner." Hank?

510
00:23:35.205 --> 00:23:38.040
You bought 51% of the company.

511
00:23:38.041 --> 00:23:39.917
Yes. but that would be bragging.

512
00:23:39.918 --> 00:23:41.586
It ain't trickin' if you got it.

513
00:23:43.213 --> 00:23:45.215
[♪ "Mainstreet" continues playing]

514
00:23:46.800 --> 00:23:48.968
<i>♪ Down on Mainstreet ♪</i>

515
00:23:48.969 --> 00:23:51.011
Welcome back. Honey.

516
00:23:51.012 --> 00:23:52.638
[phone ringing]

517
00:23:52.639 --> 00:23:55.307
Hank Hill. assistant--
uh. Hank Hill.

518
00:23:55.308 --> 00:23:58.269
manager and owner
of Strickland Propane.

519
00:23:58.270 --> 00:23:59.979
How can I help ya?

520
00:23:59.980 --> 00:24:02.274
Bill? How drunk are you?

521
00:24:02.983 --> 00:24:06.194
[♪ bluegrass version
of "Yahoos and Triangles" playing]

522
00:24:21.585 --> 00:24:24.129
<i>- ♪ Yee-haw! ♪
- ♪ Wa-hoo! ♪</i>

523
00:24:42.272 --> 00:24:43.355
[♪ song ends]

524
00:24:43.356 --> 00:24:44.440
[birds chirping]

525
00:24:44.441 --> 00:24:46.358
- [golf club thumps]
- [crowd cheering]

526
00:24:46.359 --> 00:24:48.402
♪

527
00:24:48.403 --> 00:24:51.405
[Peggy Hill]
<i>It is time for you to nut up. Bobby Hill!</i>

528
00:24:51.406 --> 00:24:54.409
[♪ fanfare playing]
